+ * Looked up by the English the code says, like muse_lang.c. Two rules the
+ * table has to live inside, both from what this screen actually is:
+ *
+ *   Width. A row's name gets about 124 px once its icon and its value label
+ *   (capped at 130 px) have taken theirs, and in the one size Chinese draws
+ *   here - 16 px - that is seven characters. A value gets eight. Every row
+ *   name below is counted, not estimated; the ones that came close went to
+ *   four or five characters instead of six.
+ *
+ *   Glyphs. CONFIG_MUSE_UI_LANG_ZH can only be picked with
+ *   CONFIG_MUSE_CARPET_CARDS, which is the only thing that pulls
+ *   muse_font_cjk_noto_16 into the image. That font is 16 px and covers
+ *   GB2312's 6763 hanzi plus U+3000-30FF and U+FF00-FFEF - so full-width
+ *   punctuation (，。、；：？！（）「」) is there and the general-punctuation
+ *   ellipsis U+2026 and em-dash U+2014 are not. "..." and "-" stay ASCII; a
+ *   missing glyph is a hollow box, and the box is what a viewer remembers.
+ *
+ * The long English help paragraphs are rewritten short rather than translated
+ * line by line: muse_text_showable() folds anything with a non-ASCII byte
+ * through a 96-byte buffer, and a 300-byte paragraph of 16 px Chinese is ten
+ * lines in a 330 px column nobody scrolls on purpose.
+ */
